## Getting started

```bash
<%= install %>
cp .env.example .env
<% if (has.docker && (hasDb || has.redis)) { -%>
docker compose up -d<%= hasDb ? ' db' : '' %><%= has.redis ? ' redis' : '' %>   # start the database locally
<% } -%>
<% if (database === 'prisma') { -%>
<%= run('db:migrate') %>                # create the tables
<% } -%>
<% if (database === 'drizzle') { -%>
<%= run('db:push') %>                   # create the tables
<% } -%>
<%= run('dev') %>
```

The API runs at http://localhost:3000<% if (has.swagger) { %> and the interactive docs at http://localhost:3000/docs<% } %>.
<% if (!has.docker && hasDb) { -%>

You need a running <%= isPostgres ? 'PostgreSQL' : 'MongoDB' %> server. Put its connection string in `DATABASE_URL` inside `.env`.
<% } -%>

## Scripts

| Script | What it does |
| ------ | ------------ |
| `<%= run('dev') %>` | Start in watch mode (restarts on save) |
<% if (isTs) { -%>
| `<%= run('build') %>` | Compile to `dist/` |
<% } -%>
| `<%= run('start') %>` | Run in production mode |
| `<%= run('test') %>` | Run the test suite once |
| `<%= run('test:watch') %>` | Run tests on every change |
| `<%= run('lint') %>` | Lint the code |
| `<%= run('format') %>` | Format all files with Prettier |
<% if (isTs) { -%>
| `<%= run('typecheck') %>` | Type-check without emitting |
<% } -%>
<% if (database === 'prisma') { -%>
| `<%= run('db:migrate') %>` | Create and apply a migration after editing `prisma/schema.prisma` |
| `<%= run('db:deploy') %>` | Apply pending migrations (production) |
| `<%= run('db:studio') %>` | Browse the data in Prisma Studio |
<% } -%>
<% if (database === 'drizzle') { -%>
| `<%= run('db:generate') %>` | Generate a SQL migration after editing `src/db/schema.<%= ext %>` |
| `<%= run('db:migrate') %>` | Apply migrations |
| `<%= run('db:push') %>` | Push the schema directly (quick local prototyping) |
| `<%= run('db:studio') %>` | Browse the data in Drizzle Studio |
<% } -%>

